able debian of our story  sentences is to take in a sentence like  mayday dreams of being a doctor where uh  may is portrayed in you know very  passively with low agency  and we're going to rewrite it to may  pursues her dream to be a doctor where  may all of a sudden has a much higher  agency uh than before  so there's actually two challenges to  doing this kind of thing um the first  one is that contrary to some existing  sort of work on uh rewriting we cannot  just paraphrase the sentences because a  lot of times the biases are actually  um  not just in the framing of the actions  that are attributed to characters but  actually in the actions themselves  um  and so on the other hand we also want to  avoid making unnecessary meaning changes  and completely rewriting the sentence so  we want to preserve as much of the  meaning as we can while also still  de-biasing  and so what you want is targeted edits  with minimal meaning change  a second challenge is that this is  essentially an unsupervised task um and  what i mean by that is that there's no  parallel input output pairs that can  show a model like this is exactly what  you should rewrite this sentence to um  and so the way that people have tackled  this problem before is using generator  discriminator models by uh basically  setting up like uh you know  discriminated on top of your generation  model and kind of like gans style things  um  but  oftentimes research has shown that this  leads to really you know disfluent or  less grammatical output text  and so our approach is um we're gonna  you follow leonal's approach of masking  and reconstructing sentences  um but in order to really do this fully  we have to add two novel modeling  aspects to this um the first one is we  added an additional paraphrasing  training objective and then at um  testing time or at generation time we're  going to add a vocabulary boosting  mechanism to reach the desired agency  levels better  all right so let me walk you through the  way that power transformer is set up  so the way this model works is we start  with an input sentence um like may  daydreams of being a doctor and a  desired agency level in this case like  high agency  um we're gonna mask all the agency  markers from the input sentence using  our connotation frames  we're going to transform our desired  agency level into a special token  we're going to feed those into a  transformer based conditional language  model in this case initializes gpt and  then at training time we're going to use  our joint reconstruction and  paraphrasing objective and then at test  time or generation time we're going to  use our vocab boosting mechanism on top  of the probabilities that are given to  us by the model  to even further reach the desired agency  level  so to be a little bit more specific the  joint training objective has two parts  the first one is an  in-domain reconstruction objective which  takes in sentences from our story corpus  uh masks the agency markers and then  optimizes the log likelihood of the  reconstructed sentence  and then the second one is an out of  domain paraphrasing objective which  basically uses pairs of paraphrases from  tv subtitles so very different corpus uh  very different domain and then optimizes  the likelihood of a sentence given its  mass paraphrase  and then the way that our decoding time  uh that our vocab boosting mechanism  works is essentially it's going to  increase the likelihood of tokens that  are connoting the right desired agency  levels  and we're doing that by adding a vocab  size vector  to um for the right agency levels at  each decoding time step  so basically like every time we generate  a new word we're going to shift the  probabilities up of the words that are  kind of in the right direction of the  right agency  um and then we can do this shifting at  different strengths using a parameter  beta here  um so there's a lot of different  components in this model right so we can  actually